/bin/
/.state/
/coverage.out
/agent-commons
/CONNECTION-EVIDENCE.md
/LIVE-EVIDENCE.md
/WAKEUP.md
*.token
/dist/
.DS_Store
# .certification/ mixes authored inputs with generated output. Ignore the
# directory's contents and re-include only what a person wrote, because certify
# reads config from exactly one path (.certification/config.yml) with no
# fallback and swallows the load error, so an untracked config silently
# degrades CI to zero policy packs and an empty policy_version.
# Deny-then-allow rather than a bare /.certification/: git does not descend into
# an excluded directory, so a negation under one never matches. Everything not
# named below stays ignored, including records/, reports/, state.json,
# index.json, queue.json, badge.json, runs.jsonl and REPORT_CARD.md.
/.certification/*
!/.certification/config.yml
!/.certification/policies/
!/.certification/overrides/
/.claude/worktrees/
